recovery of the Q1.15 accuracy drop (positive = better, negative = worse)
  baseline drop                    +4.78 %p
  B: weights only                  +3.15 %p
  C: pre-activation range only     -4.07 %p
  D: both                          +4.77 %p
  interaction (D - B - C)          +5.69 %p

  The two error sources are NOT additive. Widening the pre-activation
  range alone (C) lets the still-clipped weights push larger, more
  distorted values through tanh, so it lands below the baseline.
  Q4.12 works because it removes both sources at the same time.
